item.gvco_field_manual.name=GVCO Field Manual
gvc.military.gui.field_manual=Field Manual
gvc.manual.title=GVCO Field Manual
gvc.manual.start.title=Your first recruit
gvc.manual.start.body=Visit a military trader at a friendly camp or village outpost. Defense Corps and Free Company are friendly to new players by default. Check Factions for your current standing.\n\nOpen Military from the inventory or run /military. Deposit coins in Treasury and food in Supplies. Hire a basic infantry unit from the trader and use Personnel to find the new recruit.\n\nIssue Follow me before setting out. Check the Overview to see how long your supplies will last.
gvc.manual.recruit.title=Coins and recruiting
gvc.manual.recruit.body=Coins come from loot, server rewards, and some hostile infantry. Deposit them in Treasury. You can withdraw coins in several denominations.\n\nSelect a unit at a trader to see its equipment, price, wage, food cost, and any unlock requirements. Higher standing opens more tiers and can reduce prices.\n\nA successful hire spawns the recruit near the trader. Make room around the post if there is no suitable place to deploy the unit.
gvc.manual.upkeep.title=Keep troops supplied
gvc.manual.upkeep.body=Deposit food in Supplies. Nutrition determines how many supply points the deposit adds. The slot preview shows the value before you confirm.\n\nUpkeep takes coins and food from your account on a schedule. Review the daily totals and reserve estimate in Overview. Unloaded units can still cost upkeep, depending on the server.\n\nShortages can slow units and affect weapon handling. Servers can also enable desertion after a sustained shortage.
gvc.manual.groups.title=Organize a group
gvc.manual.groups.body=Open Personnel, then Military groups. Create a group with +. Select the new group on the right, Ctrl-click soldiers on the left, and choose Assign.\n\nUse View group to filter the roster. Choose Unassigned and Assign to remove personnel from a group. Deleting the group also returns its members to Unassigned.\n\nSelect an officer in the group to set its leader. Hover the group summary for composition and capacity. Set a quick slot to select the group during battle.
gvc.manual.orders.title=Give your first order
gvc.manual.orders.body=Aim your crosshair before opening a command interface. Hold %s for the command wheel. Left-click a sector to select it. Right-click goes back. Release the key to return to normal controls.\n\nPress %s for quick orders. Press 0 for Everyone, 1 to 8 for assigned slots, or 9 for Ungrouped. Tab lets you browse all groups. Pick a category and then the numbered order.\n\nA confirmation tells you how many soldiers accepted the order. Position orders also show a temporary marker.
gvc.manual.formation.title=Movement and engagement
gvc.manual.formation.body=Follow and Regroup bring troops to you. Hold anchors the group at its leader. Wait leaves troops in place between engagements.\n\nAim at a block for Move, Defend, or Patrol. Defend limits where the group engages. Patrol runs between the start and your marked point. Aim at a living opponent for Attack.\n\nUse Cease fire before moving past a contact. Fire at will restores engagement. Formation changes spacing independently of the current order.
gvc.manual.standing.title=Build faction standing
gvc.manual.standing.body=Check Factions for the reputation score, standing, discount, and next threshold. A faction can trust one player and oppose another in the same world.\n\nKilling a faction member lowers its reputation with you. Its actual enemies can reward the kill. Direct and troop-owned credits depend on server rules. Repeated replacement and hired targets can be restricted.\n\nTraders show offers you have yet to unlock. Check the listed reputation and allegiance requirements if a unit is locked.
gvc.manual.allegiance.title=Pledge or renounce
gvc.manual.allegiance.body=Open Allegiance while talking to the faction's military trader. Once you meet its threshold, review the terms and confirm the pledge.\n\nPledged players can receive member discounts, qualify for exclusive recruits, and claim defeated posts where allowed. You can have one pledge at a time.\n\nUse Factions to renounce or another eligible trader to switch. Review the cooldown and reputation consequences. The forces you already hired remain yours.
gvc.manual.capture.title=Resolve a settlement
gvc.manual.capture.body=Defeat the defenders and contest a hostile beacon until its control reaches zero. A neutralized site stops military trade and replacement units. Ordinary villagers can trade again when no occupation restriction applies.\n\nA pledged commander can open Factions, choose Nearby settlement, and confirm Claim for faction at an eligible beacon. Future reinforcements and offers come from the new faction.\n\nUnaligned commanders can neutralize hostile posts. Player respawning uses vanilla rules by default.
